---
title: Compilation
summary: How a subgraph is lowered to a straight-line CompiledSequence that serves all four differentiation passes, with an epoch-keyed cache, cut compilation at interior frontiers, and slot liveness.
order: 6
---

Evaluating a model by walking its graph node by node would be slow. Skoro instead **compiles** the
part of the graph a query needs into a `CompiledSequence`: a flat, index-based list of steps.

## One sequence, four passes

`compile_backward_from(&targets)` finds everything the targets depend on, sorts it
topologically, and lowers each node to one `CompiledStep`. The same sequence runs all four passes
(`forward`, `jvp_forward`, `vjp_forward`, `hvp_forward`), and the caller picks one by which method
it invokes.

## Caching, keyed by epoch

Compiled sequences are cached. A target list alone is **not** a sound key: `observe`,
`demote_to_parameter` and `remove` change a node's kind or value at a fixed `Id`, which changes which
inputs are differentiable, and so the compiled program. The key is `(epoch, targets)`, and the graph
bumps its epoch on every such mutation.

Repeated evaluation without mutation (a Fisher-scoring loop, for example) benefits. A workload that
mutates every tick (a sliding window) clears the cache every tick and gains nothing. That is
expected.

## Cut compilation

`compile_between(&cuts, &targets)` stops the traversal at a frontier of interior nodes whose values
the caller supplies, and still differentiates with respect to that frontier.

> [!WARNING] The trap
> A cut boundary must **not** lower to a constant step. If it did, everything downstream would be
> marked non-differentiable, and the values would come back right while the derivatives came back
> silently wrong. Cut nodes lower to a dedicated `Given` step: a leaf whose value is supplied and
> whose cotangent is collected, like a parameter.

`Graph::support(id)` is the forward counterpart: the nodes that depend on `id`, sorted for
determinism.

## Slot liveness

Each operation slot is released at the last step that reads it, a fact computed at compile time
(`CompiledSequence::last_use`). Only operation slots are dropped. Leaf slots stay alive, because
the VJP pass reads them after the tape has run.

> [!NOTE]
> The full design, including the tests that pin each failure mode, is in
> [`docs/graph-compiler.md`](https://github.com/mvarble/skoro/blob/main/docs/graph-compiler.md).
